=== README.md
     1	# Tennis Club Reservations
     2	
     3	REST API for managing a tennis club: surface types, courts and court reservations with price calculation,
     4	plus JWT-secured user management. Built with Spring Boot 3.5, Hibernate 6 (plain JPA, no Spring Data),
     5	H2 in-memory database and Liquibase migrations. Full design: [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).
     6	
     7	## Requirements
     8	
     9	- JDK 21 (Maven is bundled via the wrapper `./mvnw`)
    10	
    11	## Build, test, run
    12	
    13	```bash
    14	./mvnw verify                                             # compile, tests, ArchUnit, JaCoCo (90 %) check
    15	./mvnw spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.profiles=dev     # run with H2 console and initial data enabled
    16	```
    17	
    18	Swagger UI: `http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html`, H2 console (dev profile): `http://localhost:8080/h2-console`.
    19	
    20	## Configuration
    21	
    22	All `app.*` properties can be overridden with environment variables.
    23	
    24	| Property | Env variable | Default | Description |
    25	|----------|--------------|---------|-------------|
    26	| `app.data-init.enabled` | `APP_DATA_INIT_ENABLED` | `false` (`true` in `dev`) | create default surface types and courts at startup |
    27	| `app.security.jwt.secret` | `APP_JWT_SECRET` | insecure placeholder | HS256 secret, at least 32 bytes |
    28	| `app.security.jwt.access-token-validity` | `APP_SECURITY_JWT_ACCESS_TOKEN_VALIDITY` | `PT15M` | access token lifetime (ISO-8601 duration) |
    29	| `app.security.jwt.refresh-token-validity` | `APP_SECURITY_JWT_REFRESH_TOKEN_VALIDITY` | `P7D` | refresh token lifetime |
    30	| `app.security.admin.enabled` | `APP_SECURITY_ADMIN_ENABLED` | `true` | create bootstrap ADMIN account |
    31	| `app.security.admin.phone-number` | `APP_SECURITY_ADMIN_PHONE_NUMBER` | `+420000000000` | admin login |
    32	| `app.security.admin.name` | `APP_SECURITY_ADMIN_NAME` | `Administrator` | admin display name |
    33	| `app.security.admin.password` | `APP_ADMIN_PASSWORD` | `admin` | admin password |
